      "content": "Including specific cultural norms in a de-escalation module is appropriate, provided they are presented as common communication styles rather than generalized stereotypes about entire communities. It is highly effective to teach officers about behaviors such as indirect refusal to authority figures or prolonged eye contact, which can be culturally specific and should not be mistaken for defiance or threat. By familiarizing officers with these universal cultural variations, they can recognize them as non-threatening signals rather than relying on their own unconscious biases. This approach maintains accuracy without labeling any group as inherently aggressive, ensuring the training empowers understanding rather than fostering prejudice.",
